Objective:

 Exploit disabled Kerberos pre-authentication to obtain offline-crackable AS-REP hashes
 without any domain credentials.

Why It Works:

 Kerberos pre-authentication requires a client to prove knowledge of their password before the KDC will issue an AS-REP.
 If pre-auth is disabled on an account, the KDC will issue an AS-REP to anyone who asks — no credential needed.
 The AS-REP contains data encrypted with the target account's own key (password-derived),
 which can be cracked offline.

Key difference from Kerberoasting:

 . Kerberoasting targets the TGS exchange — requires a valid authenticated session first
 . AS-REP Roasting targets the AS exchange — requires zero credentials if pre-auth is disabled

Commands:
bash 

 # Find and capture AS-REP hashes (no credentials needed if pre-auth disabled)
  impacket-GetNPUsers redteamlab.local/ -dc-ip 192.168.56.101 \
  -usersfile users.txt -no-pass -format john

 # Crack the hash
   john --format=krb5asrep --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt hash.txt
 # or
   hashcat -m 18200 hash.txt /usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt


Findings

  . asrep — pre-authentication disabled
  . AS-REP hash captured
  . Password cracked: Password123

Detection:

 . Event ID 4768 (AS-REQ) with pre-auth type 0x0 (no pre-auth) — stands out
   against normal 4768 events which show pre-auth type 0x12 or 0x17

Key Lessons:

 Pre-authentication exists specifically to prevent this attack — disabling it is a serious misconfiguration
 AS-REP Roasting requires zero domain credentials — just network access to the DC on port 88
 Hash format differs from Kerberoasting: $krb5asrep$ vs $krb5tgs$ — different hashcat modes (18200 vs 13100)

Interview Explanation:

 "AS-REP Roasting exploits disabled Kerberos pre-authentication.
  When pre-auth is off, the KDC issues an AS-REP to any requester without verifying their identity
  and that response contains data encrypted with the account's own password hash.
  I captured the AS-REP for the asrep account using impacket-GetNPUsers with no domain credentials,
  then cracked it offline recovering Password123."
